,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"245.43989431968296\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"245.43989431968296\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,349.3542600896861 68.2372972972973,322.97297297297297 107.92307692307692,288.6666666666667 183.62461538461537,256.0 280.74052631578945,204.78947368421052 375.1042253521127,161.5492957746479 411.2784713375796,92.19108280254773\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 223 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"349.3542600896861\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"68.2372972972973\" cy=\"322.97297297297297\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 14%&amp;#10;It rained 26% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"107.92307692307692\" cy=\"288.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 35%&amp;#10;It rained 35% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"183.62461538461537\" cy=\"256.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 63%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"280.74052631578945\" cy=\"204.78947368421052\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 90%&amp;#10;It rained 61% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"375.1042253521127\" cy=\"161.5492957746479\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 157 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.2784713375796\" cy=\"92.19108280254773\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(38%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Linkoeping the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.29) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.08).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'>0.080</td><td class='num'>16.8%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.173</td><td class='num'>16.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.222</td><td class='num'>15.2%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'>0.287</td><td class='num'>11.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":58.41086,"lon":15.62157,"n":757,"n_cities":213,"name":"Linkoeping","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":223,"obs":0.08968609865470852,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.028918918918918922,"n":74,"obs":0.16216216216216217,"sig":true},{"hi":0.24,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.14102564102564102,"n":78,"obs":0.2564102564102564,"sig":true},{"hi":0.49,"lo":0.24,"mean":0.3548717948717949,"n":78,"obs":0.34615384615384615,"sig":false},{"hi":0.78,"lo":0.49,"mean":0.6292105263157894,"n":76,"obs":0.4868421052631579,"sig":true},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.78,"mean":0.895774647887324,"n":71,"obs":0.6056338028169014,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9979617834394905,"n":157,"obs":0.7961783439490446,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.3,"provisional":false,"rank":154,"rank_hi":173.0,"rank_lo":99.0,"reliability":0.023859599976697222,"resolution":0.07297864684571513,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"linkoeping","station":"LINKOEPING-MALMSLAETT","timezone":"Europe/Stockholm"}